    "segmentnr":"SA_K12_Āgama_Manasvināgarājasūtra_Szántó:3",
    "original":"This is the earliest hard evidence for any rakṣā text. The texts from the Bajaur Collection can be dated to the first two centuries of our era. The nāga-king Manasvin approaches the Buddha and hands him over a special mantra to be used in all kinds of calamities. Only five excerpts published in this article. Concludes that it is very close to the Mahāmāyūrī (for which a Gandhari origin is posited based on a linguistic argument).",
